I divide the game into two states for purposes of wish allocation:

* Pre-castle. At this stage, any one-off wish goes on various highly
  desirable protective devices that I may well not have yet.  I'm
  vanishingly unlikely to see enough wishes to get a full AK armour set
  before the castle, but a wish will get me SoR/AoR/SDSM or GDSM/CoMR or
  a CoD or speed boots or a helm of telepathy or brilliance.
* Post-castle. At this stage, I've had the castle wand, so I've been
  able to fill in any desperate gaps in my equipment.  I'll blow one-
  off wishes on !oFH or magic markers, and keep any WoW I find handy for
  emergencies.

Now, if I can hold my current valkyrie together, I'm looking good for
not needing many wishes from the castle wand, of course, because I found
SoR, speed boots, and GoP in an armour shop in the main dungeon.  Of
course, I'm playing a dwarven valkyrie, so the GoP aren't *that*
exciting (although St:25 is always nice :).  With lawful valkyries, I
use Excalibur in preference to Mjollnir because the lower artifact damage
is balanced out by the improved reliability (in particular, bashing
through the sanctum or Astral with Mjollnir is a miserable experience)
and the fact that Mjollnir blows up wands.

